=2 Walkthrough
\**Note:** If you complete this quest, {M:Zilart Mission 14|Zilart Mission 14|Ark Angels}, will be considered completed as well.
\**!!!NOTE:!!!** You must flag this quest at the blank target in {z:The Shrine of Ru'Avitau} or you WILL NOT receive credit and will have to re-aquire another {@i:Ark Pentasphere|1550} {i:Ark Pentasphere|Ark Pentasphere|1550}.
=4 Preparation
* Enter {z:The Shrine of Ru'Avitau} from the (H-9) entrance in {z:Ru'Aun Gardens}.
** {p:Survival Guide} puts you on the path to it, if you have it.
** {p:Home Point} #5 is another fast alternative.
* Head North a short distance to find a Blank Target at (G/H-11).
* Examine the Blank Target for a cutscene.
* Examine the Blank Target **__again**__ for dialogue about how to obtain an {@i:Ark Pentasphere|1550} {i:Ark Pentasphere|Ark Pentasphere|1550}.
** Divine Might now appears in your Outlands Quests log.
* You, or someone in your group, will need to obtain an {@i:Ark Pentasphere|1550} {i:Ark Pentasphere|Ark Pentasphere|1550}.
** {i:Ark Pentaspheres|Ark Pentasphere|1550} are created by trading 1x {@i:Illuminink|1408} {i:Illuminink|Illuminink|1408} and 1x {@i:Parchment|917} {i:Parchment|Parchment|917} to the Qu'Hau Spring at (H-6) in {z:Ro'Maeve} during a full moon and between 18:00 and 06:00 game time.
** {@i:Illuminink|1408} {i:Illuminink|Illuminink|1408} drops off {m:Cursed Puppet} and {m:Magic Flagon} in {z:Ro'Maeve}.
* Trade the {@i:Ark Pentasphere|1550} {i:Ark Pentasphere|Ark Pentasphere|1550} to any of the **Shimmering Circles** in {z:La'Loff Amphitheater} to access the battlefield.

=4 Battle
* This battle has a 30 minute time limit and allows for a full alliance of 18 people will be allowed to enter.
** This battle was initially uncapped at level 75 and was relatively challenging. Level 99 players should have little to no difficulty completing this.
* You will need to defeat {m:Ark Angel MR}, {m:Ark Angel TT}, {m:Ark Angel EV}, {m:Ark Angel HM}, and {m:Ark Angel GK} in order to win.
** Everyone should bring some form of re-raise in order to minimize down time.
** The Ark Angels share alliance hate, so people should wait to re-raise until the entire alliance is down and the mobs are back at their starting position.
** If you feel like you're about to die, try to move out of the center of the arena. People left in the center of the arena are often near impossible to raise again without getting aggro.
* If you happen to have an alliance wipe, re-raise, heal, and then finish off whoever remains.
* The general strategy at level 75 was to divide and conquer. Have one tank/kiter on each mob, while the rest of the group kills the others one by one.
** Make sure someone is keeping the pets slept at all times. They can cause chaos if left alone for too long.
** The {m:Ark Angel TT} should be defeated as fast as possible because he has access to wide selection of nasty spells.
** Along with having a pet, the {m:Ark Angel MR} will also charm at least one player before she falls.
*** {p:Fealty}, light elemental resistance equipment, and magic evasion in general are effective at resisting this.
** Every time the {m:Ark Angel GK} uses {p:Meikyo Shisui}, it will try to make a Light Skill Chain. This can be prevented if {p:utsusemi|Utsusemi} absorbs any of the weaponskills.
** When fighting the {m:Ark Angel HM} it is recommended to have as many people out of {p:Mijin Gakure} range as possible. This should not be a problem for players in 99 {p:ilvl|Item level} equipment.
*** {s:Barfira} does **not** reduce {p:Mijin Gakure} damage.
** The {m:Ark Angel EV} {p:Spirits Within} is very strong and can take out someone in just one hit.
* Once you have finished the battle, return to the Blank Target in {z:The Shrine of Ru'Avitau} to choose your reward.

=4 Re-Questing
\**{c=red:Note:}**{c=red: You are only allowed to re-quest this once per }{p:Conquest Tally|Conquest}{c=red:.}
* Drop your current earring. You will need to zone if you drop it in the same area, as the game checks your Recycle Bin as part of its inspection of your various inventories. The target will be unresponsive until you do this.
* Receive the quest at the unmarked target (G/H-11) in the main entrance of {z:The Shrine of Ru'Avitau}. The game will mention your old quest reward by name and seems to track your prior selection.
* The quest appears as a second Divine Might quest in your quest log with a different description.
* Obtain a {@i:Light Ore|1261} {i:Light Ore|Light Ore|1261}.
* If you need a new {@i:Ark Pentasphere|1550} {i:Ark Pentasphere|Ark Pentasphere|1550} (an already used one will no longer work - "The Illuminink on the ark pentasphere has faded."), obtain an {@i:Illuminink|1408} {i:Illuminink|Illuminink|1408} and {@i:Parchment|917} {i:Parchment|Parchment|917} as well. This part can be done prior to accepting the actual quest.
* Trade the {@i:Light Ore|1261} {i:Light Ore|Light Ore|1261} to the Qu'Hau Spring in {z:Ro'Maeve} during a Full Moon between 18:00 and 6:00 to receive the {@k}{k:Moonlight ore}. You cannot do this until the new quest has been started.
** Warning: if you need both the {@k}{k:Moonlight ore} and the {@i:Ark Pentasphere|1550} {i:Ark Pentasphere|Ark Pentasphere|1550}, you must make TWO separate trades.
** If all three items are traded, only the {@k}{k:Moonlight ore} will be obtained.
** Each individual restarting this quest must possess their own {@k}{k:Moonlight ore}.
* Trade the {@i:Illuminink|1408} {i:Illuminink|Illuminink|1408} and {@i:Parchment|917} {i:Parchment|Parchment|917} to the Qu'Hau Spring in {z:Ro'Maeve} during a Full Moon between 18:00 and 6:00 to obtain an {@i:Ark Pentasphere|1550} {i:Ark Pentasphere|Ark Pentasphere|1550}.
** Only one alliance member needs the {@i:Ark Pentasphere|1550} {i:Ark Pentasphere|Ark Pentasphere|1550} to initiate the battle.
* Enter and complete the Divine Might battlefield at {z:La'Loff Amphitheater}.
* Return to the unmarked target in {z:The Shrine of Ru'Avitau} to pick up a new earring.

=2 Notes
* Prior to the {p:June 2016 Version Update|June 2016 Version Update Changes}, a player would have to trade their items for an {@i:Ark Pentasphere|1550} {i:Ark Pentasphere|Ark Pentasphere|1550} or {@k}{k:Moonlight ore} on a clear night during the full moon from midnight to 3:00 a.m.

